text:
This looks like leftovers. The bowl holds about 8 green grapes or grape halves in pinkish juice, roughly 40 g of grapes plus about 30 g of liquid, which comes to around 70 kcal if the liquid is a fruit-cocktail syrup. The glass holds about 100 ml of pale apple-type juice, about 45 kcal. The plate has only crumbs and a small red piece, so I count it as negligible.

Grapes at 40 g are about 28 kcal. The syrupy liquid at 30 g adds about 15 kcal. The juice at 100 g adds about 45 kcal. That totals about 88 kcal and 170 g.

